  "content": {
    "_uid": "c62f811d-7566-ae08-6d95-b2a4fca95cda",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "0f369688-2977-6d45-aded-5bc7b94ff668",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Labelling coronary artery, disease as a major cause of illness and deaths in Pakistan, Dr Pathanexplained that this disease leads to the narrowing of the blood vessels of the heart and is a slowly progressing process that may remain clinically unapparent for long periods of time. Coronary disease often becomes clinically evident because of the occurrence of symtoms such as angina or those associated with a heart attack or even sudden death. Dr Pathan stressed on the early detection of the disease and mentioned that coronary angiography is a reliable and safe procedure with a trivial but definable risk. The information obtained from angiography provides diagnostic information and is invaluable in making appropriate decisions about therapeutic interventions such as angioplasty or bypass surgery, which leads to relief of angina and can improve the long term outcome in some patients. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "A panel of Consultant Cardiologists also participated in the panel discussion. This included Dr Khawar Abbass Kazmi, Dr Anwar Ahmed and Dr Momina Mastoor.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
