    "show_share": true,
    "description": "\"Coronary angiography was first performed 40 years ago, and remains the gold standard test for diagnosis of coronary artery disease, against which other diagnostic tests arc validated\", revealed Dr Asad Pathan. Consultant Clinical and Interventional Cardiologist of the Aga Khan University Hospital (AKUH). He was giving a presentation on \"Coronary Angiography\" at \"Signs, Symptoms and Care\", a monthly public health awareness program, held on May 8. 1999 at AKUH Dr Path an added, \"angiography is currently the only established method for accurately assessing the extent and severity of coronary artery disease\",",
